{"name":"Solitude","hex":"#e9ecf1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"solitude","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Aloneness; the state of being alone, solitary, or by oneself.","A lonely or deserted place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solitude"}],"entries":[{"title":"Solitude","blocks":[{"text":"Solitude, also known as social withdrawal, is a state of seclusion or isolation, meaning lack of socialisation. Effects can be either positive or negative, depending on the situation. Short-term solitude is often valued as a time when one may work, think, or rest without disturbance. It may be desired for the sake of privacy. Long-term solitude may stem from soured relationships, loss of loved ones, deliberate choice, infectious disease, mental disorders, neurological disorders such as circadian rhythm sleep disorder, or circumstances of employment or situation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Pyle_pirate_marooned.jpg/330px-Pyle_pirate_marooned.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solitude"},{"title":"Solitude (football ground)","blocks":[{"text":"Solitude is a football stadium in north Belfast, Northern Ireland. Home ground of Ireland's oldest football club, Cliftonville, it is the oldest football stadium in Ireland. The stadium holds 6,224, but is currently restricted to 2,530 under safety legislation with the old main stand now closed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/20190112_Solitude_outside.jpg/330px-20190112_Solitude_outside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solitude_(football_ground)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/%D7%97%D7%A1%D7%99%D7%93_%D7%9E%D7%AA%D7%91%D7%95%D7%93%D7%93.jpg/500px-%D7%97%D7%A1%D7%99%D7%93_%D7%9E%D7%AA%D7%91%D7%95%D7%93%D7%93.